Use this command only from an active ready configuration `itldev/*` worktree.

Run the helper directly from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second 1C Designer/Enterprise limit. Do not use `120000 ms` or another short default.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action reset-dev-branch
```

The helper checkpoints the branch, creates and verifies a resumable archive with the current infobase DT and non-configuration files, creates a normal cleanup commit whose tree exactly equals the current local `master`, and recreates the branch infobase from the matching seed. Repeat the same command after an interrupted reset; do not repair Git, the journal, or the infobase manually. On success with a non-empty `userReport`, return it exactly as Russian Markdown, including the absolute archive and DT paths. On failure, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath`.
